    "reply": "PMID 11237011 has a broad set of MeSH annotations covering genome sequencing, genome structure, evolution and medical genetics. The assigned terms include Genome, Human [14] and Human Genome Project [15]. They also include Sequence Analysis, DNA [20].\n\n## Genome Structure Terms\n\nSeveral terms describe genomic sequence features. These are Repetitive Sequences, Nucleic Acid [11] and DNA Transposable Elements [3]. The set also includes CpG Islands [21], GC Rich Sequence [25] and Conserved Sequence [17]. Chromosome Mapping is also assigned [2].\n\n## Evolution and Comparative Genomics\n\nEvolutionary concepts are represented by Evolution, Molecular [22] and Gene Duplication [23]. Species Specificity is assigned [13]. The organism headings are Humans [8] and Animals [1].\n\n## Genes and Gene Products\n\nThe molecular headings are Genes [6], Proteins [10], Proteome [24] and RNA [12]. Mutation is also assigned [9].\n\n## Medical and Societal Context\n\nThe clinical headings are Genetics, Medical [7] and Genetic Diseases, Inborn [26]. The organizational headings are Drug Industry [4], Private Sector [18] and Public Sector [19]. The remaining terms are Databases, Factual [16] and Forecasting [5].",
